  <p>October 20, 2026: checked product-media and Files requirements, compared theme guidance, and retained the differences in megapixels, formats, and video resolution. Checked the hubStudio export controls against its help center. The source pages are living documents without displayed revision dates; the date here records when they were read.</p>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

  <h3>What size should Shopify product images be?</h3>

  <p>For a square product image, start with Shopify’s recommended 2048 x 2048 pixels. Test the actual product page before making the batch. If the product looks too small or loses an edge, review the framing and theme crop before increasing resolution.</p>

  <h3>What is the maximum image size on Shopify?</h3>

  <p>For product media, Shopify lists 5000 x 5000 pixels or 25 MP, below 20 MB. Both limits matter: a compact file can still contain too many pixels. Theme-image documentation has different wording, explained above. Keep a master copy and test the intended upload surface before preparing large exports for the whole catalog.</p>

  <h3>Should Shopify product images be square?</h3>

  <p>Shopify’s size recommendation applies when you choose a square image; it doesn’t require that shape. The object and its display area should guide the ratio. Keep main images consistent across a collection, then check whether secondary views need a different crop to show the detail clearly.</p>

  <h3>What image formats does Shopify accept?</h3>

  <p>JPEG, PNG, WebP, HEIC, and GIF appear in both the Files and product-media lists. Shopify’s product-media page also names additional formats, with conversion and transformation qualifications elsewhere in its help center. Transparency or animation can change how an image looks after upload, so inspect the preview before approving the batch.</p>

  <h3>Why are my Shopify product images cropped?</h3>

  <p>The image’s shape may differ from the area where the theme displays it. Look at the affected section on desktop and on a phone. If its settings offer no suitable adjustment, prepare a crop that keeps the product inside its visible area without stretching it.</p>

  <h3>Can I add video to a Shopify product page?</h3>

  <p>Yes, provided the theme supports product video. Uploaded files can run up to 10 minutes and 1 GB; check the resolution distinction above. Test playback after upload, including the opening frame. A file that transfers successfully but has no working preview needs investigation before you use it across the rest of the catalog.</p>

  <p>Make a product image and check the exported file in your storefront.</p>
